<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21022] fld: use an interval tree for the FLD cache</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21022</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;fld_cache_lookup()&lt;/tt&gt; is a linear scan of the sorted &lt;tt&gt;fci_entries_head&lt;/tt&gt; list under the global &lt;tt&gt;fci_lock&lt;/tt&gt;, called on hot paths such as cross-MDT lock and getattr for every FLD resolution once patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69555" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69555&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20923" title="servers should reject invalid FIDs, requests, ..." class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20923"&gt;LU-20923&lt;/a&gt; mdt: refuse new objects with non-MDT FIDs") is landed.  The cache holds sequence ranges &lt;tt&gt;[lsr_start, lsr_end)&lt;/tt&gt; mapped to a target, so lookup is an interval (range-containing) query.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Replace the sorted linked list with a kernel interval tree (&lt;tt&gt;INTERVAL_TREE_DEFINE&lt;/tt&gt; from &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;linux/interval_tree_generic.h&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;, as &lt;tt&gt;lustre/obdclass/range_lock.c&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;lustre/ptlrpc/nodemap_range.c&lt;/tt&gt; already use) for O(log n) lookup, insert and delete while keeping the merge/split-on-overlap semantics and the LRU shrink list.  A hash table is not suitable because the ranges are variable width (adjacent same-target ranges are merged) so there is no fixed key to hash.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
